  "description": "Find the minimum and maximum moves to place stones in consecutive positions given their initial coordinates.",
  "target": null,
  "pseudocode": "1. sort(stones)\n2. n = stones.length\n3. max_moves = max(stones[n-1]-stones[1]-n+2, stones[n-2]-stones[0]-n+2)\n4. min_moves = n\n5. left = 0\n6. for right from 0 to n-1:\n7.   while stones[right] - stones[left] >= n:\n8.     left++\n9.   if right - left + 1 == n - 1 and stones[right] - stones[left] == n - 2:\n10.    min_moves = min(min_moves, 2)\n11.  else:\n12.    min_moves = min(min_moves, n - (right - left + 1))",
